WEBVTT

0
00:00.142 --> 00:02.071
<v Krista>In this video we are talking about multiplication</v>

1
00:02.071 --> 00:03.048
of signed numbers.

2
00:03.048 --> 00:04.458
And when we say signed numbers,

3
00:04.458 --> 00:06.398
we're just talking about numbers with either

4
00:06.398 --> 00:08.787
a positive sign or a negative sign attached.

5
00:08.787 --> 00:11.505
For example, in this expression we have here,

6
00:11.505 --> 00:14.099
two is a positive number and three is a negative number

7
00:14.099 --> 00:15.957
with the negative sign in front here.

8
00:15.957 --> 00:17.639
So when we want to multiply either

9
00:17.639 --> 00:19.337
two positive numbers together,

10
00:19.337 --> 00:20.982
two negative numbers together,

11
00:20.982 --> 00:23.398
or a mix of positive and negative numbers,

12
00:23.398 --> 00:25.606
what will be the sign of the result?

13
00:25.606 --> 00:28.072
Well, we have this chart here to help us remember

14
00:28.072 --> 00:29.870
what the sign of the result will be.

15
00:29.870 --> 00:31.376
What we're saying with this chart is that

16
00:31.376 --> 00:35.503
if we multiply together a positive and a positive number,

17
00:35.503 --> 00:37.545
we find the inner section of these two,

18
00:37.545 --> 00:39.139
we're going to get a positive number.

19
00:39.139 --> 00:41.786
Or if we multiply together a negative number and

20
00:41.786 --> 00:44.764
a negative number, we're going to get a positive number.

21
00:44.764 --> 00:47.389
If on the other hand we multiply a negative number

22
00:47.389 --> 00:50.149
by a positive number, we get a negative number.

23
00:50.149 --> 00:52.465
And if we multiply a positive number

24
00:52.465 --> 00:55.300
by a negative number, we get a negative number.

25
00:55.300 --> 00:57.270
Another way to remember this is that if we are

26
00:57.270 --> 00:58.971
multiplying two numbers together

27
00:58.971 --> 01:02.376
and they have the same sign, if the sign is the same,

28
01:02.376 --> 01:04.719
then the result will be positive.

29
01:04.719 --> 01:06.639
If we are multiplying two numbers together

30
01:06.639 --> 01:08.825
and their signs are different,

31
01:08.825 --> 01:11.701
the result will always be negative.

32
01:11.701 --> 01:14.218
So two different signs, the result will always be negative.

33
01:14.218 --> 01:17.111
Two of the same signs, the result will always be positive.

34
01:17.111 --> 01:19.465
And it doesn't matter if we have two positive numbers

35
01:19.465 --> 01:20.668
that are being multiplied together

36
01:20.668 --> 01:23.399
or two negative numbers that are being multiplied together.

37
01:23.399 --> 01:26.211
They have the same sign, so the result will be positive.

38
01:26.211 --> 01:28.812
So, if we apply this logic to these expressions

39
01:28.812 --> 01:31.410
we've been given here to find the result, what do we get?

40
01:31.410 --> 01:33.004
Well, we have two times three.

41
01:33.004 --> 01:34.641
Those are both positive numbers.

42
01:34.641 --> 01:37.053
We have positive two times positive three.

43
01:37.053 --> 01:38.906
The signs are the same, they are both positive.

44
01:38.906 --> 01:41.154
So our result is going to be positive,

45
01:41.154 --> 01:43.064
our result will be six.

46
01:43.064 --> 01:45.744
Here we have positive two times a negative three.

47
01:45.744 --> 01:47.083
We have a positive and a negative,

48
01:47.083 --> 01:48.227
their signs are different.

49
01:48.227 --> 01:49.710
We know that if we have different signs,

50
01:49.710 --> 01:51.121
the result will be negative.

51
01:51.121 --> 01:52.832
So, we get negative six.

52
01:52.832 --> 01:54.219
Here we switch the order,

53
01:54.219 --> 01:56.118
we have negative two and a positive three.

54
01:56.118 --> 01:58.316
But the point is we have a negative number

55
01:58.316 --> 01:59.455
and a positive number.

56
01:59.455 --> 02:01.542
Different signs so the result is negative

57
02:01.542 --> 02:02.985
and we get negative six.

58
02:02.985 --> 02:04.586
And here we have two negative numbers

59
02:04.586 --> 02:06.431
negative two and negative three,

60
02:06.431 --> 02:08.680
the signs are the same, they're both negative.

61
02:08.680 --> 02:10.768
So our result is positive.

62
02:10.768 --> 02:13.199
Now keep in mind that this logic only applies

63
02:13.199 --> 02:16.973
when you're multiplying together just two signed numbers.

64
02:16.973 --> 02:19.392
If you're multiplying together more than two numbers,

65
02:19.392 --> 02:21.296
you have three numbers that you're multiplying together,

66
02:21.296 --> 02:23.299
or four numbers you're multiplying together,

67
02:23.299 --> 02:25.491
this logic doesn't necessarily hold.

68
02:25.491 --> 02:28.115
So, for example, if I want to multiply together

69
02:28.115 --> 02:32.508
negative two, times negative three, times negative four,

70
02:32.508 --> 02:35.113
or if I want to multiply together negative two,

71
02:35.113 --> 02:38.768
times negative three, times negative four,

72
02:38.768 --> 02:42.592
times negative five, our results are going to be different.

73
02:42.592 --> 02:45.602
So here I have negative two, negative three, negative four.

74
02:45.602 --> 02:48.094
You might say, well the signs are all the same,

75
02:48.094 --> 02:48.996
they're all negative.

76
02:48.996 --> 02:50.837
So my result is going to be positive,

77
02:50.837 --> 02:52.219
because my signs are the same.

78
02:52.219 --> 02:53.349
But that's not true.

79
02:53.349 --> 02:55.660
The reason that this logic works when we have two numbers

80
02:55.660 --> 02:59.442
is because for every two negative signs you have,

81
02:59.442 --> 03:00.560
they're going to cancel each other out

82
03:00.560 --> 03:01.587
and become a positive.

83
03:01.587 --> 03:03.666
So here I have negative two, times negative three,

84
03:03.666 --> 03:04.946
I have two negative signs.

85
03:04.946 --> 03:07.428
So I can cancel out my two negative signs.

86
03:07.428 --> 03:09.487
And I can turn them into positive signs

87
03:09.487 --> 03:11.859
and now I have positive two, times positive three.

88
03:11.859 --> 03:14.186
Which of course we know was the positive six.

89
03:14.186 --> 03:16.498
The reason the result of these two examples

90
03:16.498 --> 03:20.127
was a negative six, is because I had only one negative sign.

91
03:20.127 --> 03:22.829
In other words, I had an odd number of negative signs,

92
03:22.829 --> 03:24.896
and so my result was negative.

93
03:24.896 --> 03:26.911
So really our conclusion needs to be,

94
03:26.911 --> 03:29.080
if you have an even number

95
03:29.080 --> 03:33.858
of negative signs, then the result is going to be positive.

96
03:33.858 --> 03:37.738
If you have an odd number of negative signs,

97
03:37.738 --> 03:39.853
then the result is going to be negative.

98
03:39.853 --> 03:41.683
So here we can see why that works.

99
03:41.683 --> 03:43.752
We have a negative two and a negative three.

100
03:43.752 --> 03:47.481
We know that we can cancel out every two negative signs.

101
03:47.481 --> 03:49.609
So we can turn both of these into positives.

102
03:49.609 --> 03:51.562
This negative sign doesn't have another one

103
03:51.562 --> 03:52.795
that we can cancel it with,

104
03:52.795 --> 03:54.107
so it's just going to stay there.

105
03:54.107 --> 03:55.829
We know two times three is six,

106
03:55.829 --> 03:59.271
so we get six times a negative four,

107
03:59.271 --> 04:02.125
and we know that that's going to be negative 24.

108
04:02.125 --> 04:03.993
So you can see that the result was negative

109
04:03.993 --> 04:06.563
because we had an odd number of negative signs.

110
04:06.563 --> 04:10.335
We had one, two, three negative signs, an odd number.

111
04:10.335 --> 04:12.396
Because we have an odd number of negative signs,

112
04:12.396 --> 04:13.795
the result was negative.

113
04:13.795 --> 04:16.089
In this case, negative two, times negative three,

114
04:16.089 --> 04:17.979
times negative four, times negative five.

115
04:17.979 --> 04:19.919
We have an even number of negative signs, right?

116
04:19.919 --> 04:22.984
One, two, three, four negative signs.

117
04:22.984 --> 04:25.031
So we expect our result to be positive.

118
04:25.031 --> 04:27.052
And in fact, that's true because we can cancel

119
04:27.052 --> 04:28.438
every two negative signs.

120
04:28.438 --> 04:30.969
So one, two negative signs become a positive.

121
04:30.969 --> 04:33.519
One, two negative signs become a positive.

122
04:33.519 --> 04:35.559
And now we have all positive numbers.

123
04:35.559 --> 04:37.449
So two times three is six.

124
04:37.449 --> 04:39.258
Four times five is 20.

125
04:39.258 --> 04:43.008
Six times 20 is 120, and that's positive 120.

126
04:44.515 --> 04:46.099
So, our result is positive

127
04:46.099 --> 04:48.522
because we had an even number of negative signs.

128
04:48.522 --> 04:50.605
And that's how you deal with multiplication

129
04:50.605 --> 04:52.105
of signed numbers.